==Etymology==
NRG's name is a [[wikipedia:gramogram|gramogram]] of the word "energy", which references his energy output.

NRG could also refer to [[Wikipedia: NRG Energy|NRG Energy, Inc]], a large American energy company founded in 1992, whose portfolio includes nuclear generation.

==Trivia==
*Even though Prime Timeline version of NRG first appeared in ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'' on November 12, 2010, NRG's actual debut took place in ''[[Ben 10 Franklin]]'', which originally aired on November 1, 2010.
*NRG is the only [[Andromeda (Classic)|Andromeda]] alien to not be based on an animal, as [[Terraspin]] is a cross between a [[Wikipedia:Tortoise|tortoise]] and a [[Wikipedia:Turtle|turtle]], [[Waterhazard]] is a [[Wikipedia:Mollusca|mollusk]], [[Ampfibian (Classic)|Ampfibian]] is a [[Wikipedia:Jellyfish|jellyfish]], and [[Armodrillo]] is an [[Wikipedia:Armadillo|armadillo]].
**However, like the other Andromeda aliens, he has powers linked to a certain classical element; for NRG, it is fire.
*NRG is tied with [[Gax]] for the shortest name for any transformation in the [[Ben 10 (Franchise)|'''Ben 10''' franchise]].
**NRG and [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]] are the only aliens whose names are gramograms.
*NRG speaks with a [[Wikipedia:Russia|Russian]] accent because Russia is known for creating many of the first nuclear weapons, and currently owns about 7,850 nuclear warheads.
*NRG was the [[Alien of the Month]] in June 2011.
*In all of the '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' episodes NRG's true form is seen, the [[Omnitrix]] symbol is on both of his containment suits, making him the only alien that has two Omnitrix symbols on his body.
*NRG retains [[P'Andor]]'s armor, even though other [[Prypiatosian-B]]s do not have it and it is not part of their genetic sequence. This is because it was added by the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] as part of a life support system to keep him from causing radiation poisoning to those who are vulnerable to his radiation.{{Refn|[[:File:Ultimate Humungousaur Can't Grow 1.PNG]]|group = DM}}
*The secondary containment suit NRG wears in '''Omniverse''' helps him keep his form and maintain safer radiation levels for a short time out of the suit.{{Refn|group = DJW|name = Archive}}
*[[Ben 23]] has an alternate counterpart of NRG.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23 Andromeda Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}
*NRG was designed by [[Steven Choi]]{{Refn|[[:File:Steven Choi designed NRG.PNG]]|group = SC}} and is partially inspired by the [[w:c:scoobydoo:10,000_Volt_Ghost|10,000 Volt Ghost]] from '''Scooby-Doo'''.{{Refn|[[:File:NRG OV Design Inspiration.png]]|group = DJW}}
*NRG bears a strong resemblance to Furnace from '''Invincible''': both have glowing lava-like humanoid bodies at their core, and a grey suit which have ventilation grill-like slits to view out of.
*NRG was originally not supposed to appear:
**A second time in ''[[The Purge]]'', with his role taken by [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/7/71/The_Purge_Script_Outline.pdf ''The Purge'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
**In the dream in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/d/d4/Night_of_the_Living_Nightmare_Script_First_Draft.pdf ''Night of the Living Nightmare'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = first}}

